{"id":"int-5a95037cd4240cd138790ceca54e2c02","kind":"field_change","created_at":"2026-08-05T23:00:23.928221Z","actor":"Richard T. Carback III","issue_id":"isingmark-rag","extra":{"field":"status","new_value":"closed","old_value":"open","reason":"Not worth the cost. The FIFO queue from isingmark-7ka removes the record-loss hazard that sweep.rs's module doc cited, but a second constraint remains: with one shared session every cell's records return in a single RunReport.records, JobRecord carries no cell identifier, and job_id is byte-identical across cells by the paired design. The queue stops records being lost; nothing says which cell a record belongs to. RunParams::jobs is also a fixed Vec<Job> handed over up front with dispatch order driven by miner-requested credits, so cells cannot be staged without changing run_session's interface. Every way to make a shared session safe (a batch/cell tag on Job and JobRecord, or a staged-jobs API) adds a JSONL field or changes reviewed session code to save one subprocess spawn per grid cell, which is bounded and small. Keeping per-cell sessions makes per-cell attribution free. isingmark-jfq updates sweep.rs's rationale to state this constraint instead of the stale HashMap-overwrite one."}}
